# Domain errors and clearance inconsistencies: SPEC sections 7.2 and 7.4.
# The range errors make this file fail; the inconsistencies are warnings.
scenario "Domain errors"

fix VOMAN 12.95 77.67
flight AI202 type A320 enter VOMAN alt FL240 hdg 090 spd 280KT
flight BA117 type B777 enter VOMAN alt FL250 hdg 270 spd 300KT

# Out of range, written as a literal.
clear AI202 heading 450

# Out of range after constant propagation: the compiler knows what h holds.
let h = 500
clear AI202 heading h

# Below the lowest modelled speed.
clear AI202 speed 60KT - 20

# Contradictory vertical clearances with no advance between them.
clear BA117 climb FL320
clear BA117 descend FL280

# Both of these assign the lateral path.
clear BA117 heading 180
clear BA117 direct VOMAN

# BA117's last altitude clearance was 'descend FL280', so FL300 really is
# upwards and this one is fine. Change it to FL260 and the compiler will say
# the climb does not climb -- it tracks the commanded level through the code.
advance 60
clear BA117 climb FL300

# Time cannot run backwards.
advance 0
